# ------------------------------- Course 3 · Section 5 (Ship the Artifact) ------
# Everything below is produced by a command in a c3-unit23..28 README, or by that
# unit's receipts.sh. Scoped per unit, exactly like the Section 2, 3 and 4 blocks
# above, because `native/`, `central/`, `wrapper/` and `templates/` are all
# plausible source directory names and a bare rule here would hide one in some
# future unit.
#
# NOT ignored, and deliberately committed:
#   c3-unit23/central/          the maven-jar-plugin metadata and directory listing
#                               `./receipts.sh release` derives its version chip from
#   c3-unit25/central/          the four GitHub action release documents and the
#                               Adoptium release list `./receipts.sh actions` reads
#   c3-unit27/central/          the native-maven-plugin metadata and the GraalVM CE
#                               release document `./receipts.sh graalvm` reads
#   c3-unit24/wrapper/          a REAL gradle-wrapper.jar, 47 KB of binary, which is
#                               the whole point of that unit's second break. The root
#                               of this file has no `*.jar` rule and must never grow
#                               one - see c3-unit24/templates/java.gitignore.
#   c3-unit25/workflows/        the taught workflow file. It is NOT at .github/ and
#                               must not be moved there by a rule.
#   c3-unit27/src/main/resources/META-INF/native-image/   reflect-config.json and
#                               resource-config.json, which are evidence, not output.
# All of those are tracked, and `git check-ignore -q` must keep returning non-zero
# for every one of them or `./receipts.sh` stops working from a clean clone.

# receipts.sh working files: one .out per block, the .raw build log behind it, the
# de-duplicated finding lists two blocks derive their counts from, and the
# throwaway trees the exercise answers and the probes run in.
